WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:12.500
My name is Kailey.

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:13.990
I have a YouTube channel called

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:15.190
thedollsintherain,

00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:17.260
and I restore American Girl dolls.

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:19.200
I'm going to walk you
through how I restore

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.930
a 1990s Felicity American Girl Doll.

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:24.430
Felicity Merriman is
one of American Girl's

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:27.100
six original historical characters.

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:28.750
Originally, this doll would have sold

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:30.210
for around $100,

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:34.350
but in its current state,
it is worth about $55.

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:35.460
After I restore her,

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:38.044
she'll probably be worth around $200.

00:00:38.044 --> 00:00:39.640
Felicity's biggest problems

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:41.870
are definitely her missing arm,

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:45.310
she has nail polish on
all of her hands and feet,

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:47.160
her hair is very messy,

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:49.351
and the face paint is faded.

00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:56.833
So, the first thing I'm doing

00:00:56.833 --> 00:00:58.876
is taking off Felicity's head.

00:00:58.876 --> 00:01:02.420
I'm doing this by untying her neck string.

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:04.690
I'm using a sewing pin to help

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:06.174
get the knot undone.

00:01:13.735 --> 00:01:14.755
Then, once it's untied,

00:01:14.755 --> 00:01:16.830
I'm just pulling off her head.

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:22.920
Now that her head is detached,

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:25.000
I'm removing all of her stuffing.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:26.450
I'm just pulling it out by hand

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:27.770
and collecting it in a pile

00:01:27.770 --> 00:01:29.895
so I can use it again later on.

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:40.270
Now that Felicity is unstuffed,

00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:42.650
I'm going to take off her limbs.

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:44.650
So I'm just untying these,

00:01:44.650 --> 00:01:46.883
and, again, I'm using a sewing pin

00:01:46.883 --> 00:01:48.634
to help undo the knots.

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:55.570
Now I have Felicity's limbs detached,

00:01:55.570 --> 00:01:57.780
and next I'll be removing the tension cups

00:01:57.780 --> 00:01:59.880
from inside of her arms and legs.

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:02.890
To do this, I'm putting
her limbs into a Ziploc bag

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:04.931
and boiling water in a kettle.

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:08.270
I want the water to be boiling hot,

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:10.133
so the vinyl melts.

00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:13.770
Once the water is boiled,

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:16.610
I'm putting the Ziploc bag into the water

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:18.770
and leaving it there for about a minute.

00:02:18.770 --> 00:02:20.500
This is going to heat up the limbs

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:22.530
so I can remove the tension cups

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:24.780
without cracking the limbs.

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:28.460
Now that the limbs are heated up,

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:31.020
I'm using a pair of needle-nose pliers

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:33.087
to pull the tension cups out.

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:49.210
Next, I'm going to be cleaning Felicity.

00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:52.230
Felicity has nail polish
on her fingernails

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:53.630
and her toenails.

00:02:53.630 --> 00:02:56.150
American Girl dolls should
not have nail polish,

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:59.609
so obviously her previous
owner has painted them.

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:05.740
To do this, I'm using
non-acetone nail-polish remover.

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:07.060
It's very important to use

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:09.210
non-acetone nail-polish remover,

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:11.640
as acetone can damage vinyl.

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:15.190
All I'm doing is putting
the nail-polish remover

00:03:15.190 --> 00:03:16.940
onto a cotton ball

00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:19.520
and rubbing the nail polish off.

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:20.880
Once I have most of it off,

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:22.575
I'm using a fine Q-tip

00:03:22.575 --> 00:03:25.609
to get into the crevices of the nails.

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:32.990
Now that all of the nail polish is off,

00:03:32.990 --> 00:03:34.677
I'm using a Magic Eraser

00:03:34.677 --> 00:03:36.852
to clean the rest of her skin.

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:47.398
Over time, American Girl
dolls can get very dirty.

00:03:47.398 --> 00:03:49.640
You can see this when they are shiny.

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:51.330
It's just a collection of grease

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:53.747
and sometimes the oil from your hands.

00:03:58.390 --> 00:04:00.840
I'm also using a Magic Eraser on her face,

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.520
but I'm being very careful

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:05.030
not to scrub too hard on
her lips and eyebrows,

00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:07.113
because this can remove the paint.

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:14.440
Now that Felicity is clean,

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:17.042
I'm going to restring her.

00:04:20.770 --> 00:04:23.278
Now that all of her limbs
are attached to her body,

00:04:23.278 --> 00:04:25.590
I am restuffing Felicity.

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:33.240
Once I have all of the stuffing back in,

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:35.360
I reattach Felicity's head.

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:37.310
I just put it back into the opening

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:39.143
and tie the string tight.

00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:55.520
Now I'm going to begin
fixing Felicity's hair,

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:57.210
which is one of the hardest parts

00:04:57.210 --> 00:04:59.270
of restoring an old doll.

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:01.920
Her hair is very frizzy and knotted.

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:07.415
I use a spray bottle and a wired hairbrush

00:05:07.415 --> 00:05:09.475
to help get all of the knots out.

00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:11.950
When I'm brushing doll hair,

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:14.070
I always start from the bottom of the wig

00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:15.810
and then work my way upwards,

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:17.700
so I'm not dragging down the knots

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:19.375
to the bottom of the hair.

00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:26.370
Next, I'll be straightening
Felicity's hair.

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:29.190
I'm doing this to remove the frizz.

00:05:29.190 --> 00:05:31.320
I'm making sure her hair is very wet,

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:32.530
as using a straightener

00:05:32.530 --> 00:05:35.530
on dry American Girl
doll hair can burn it.

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:46.450
I finished straightening
all of Felicity's hair,

00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:48.040
and usually I would stop there,

00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:49.860
but Felicity has pin curls

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:51.590
at the front of her head,

00:05:51.590 --> 00:05:54.080
so I need to recurl those.

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:56.360
I've straightened each
of the three pin curls,

00:05:56.360 --> 00:05:59.760
and I'm going to be using
a straw and boiling water

00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:02.435
to get them back to their original shape.

00:06:02.435 --> 00:06:05.840
I'm tying each little curl
around a plastic straw

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:08.557
and securing it in place with a bobby pin.

00:06:19.090 --> 00:06:20.750
Now I'm dipping the side of her head

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:22.660
into boiling water.

00:06:22.660 --> 00:06:25.283
I'm leaving it there for about 30 seconds,

00:06:27.910 --> 00:06:30.010
then I'm taking her head back out

00:06:30.010 --> 00:06:31.797
and leaving her to dry.

00:06:33.470 --> 00:06:35.810
Next, I'm just removing
the plastic straws,

00:06:35.810 --> 00:06:37.763
and her curls are back.

00:06:45.744 --> 00:06:47.160
Overall, Felicity's face paint

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:49.580
has definitely faded over time.

00:06:49.580 --> 00:06:50.720
Her lips are faded,

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:52.120
her teeth are faded,

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:53.130
her cheeks are faded,

00:06:53.130 --> 00:06:56.129
and there is some damage to her eyebrows.

00:06:58.620 --> 00:07:01.680
I'm using watercolors to
paint Felicity's face.

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:04.070
I think it gives the dolls
a really natural look,

00:07:04.070 --> 00:07:05.840
especially with the older dolls

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:07.790
that didn't have as dramatic makeup

00:07:07.790 --> 00:07:09.473
as the newer dolls have.

00:07:11.590 --> 00:07:13.690
I'm using a very fine paintbrush

00:07:13.690 --> 00:07:15.470
and tracing over the lips

00:07:15.470 --> 00:07:17.220
that were already there.

00:07:20.280 --> 00:07:23.010
I do this in one thin layer at a time,

00:07:23.010 --> 00:07:25.772
and then I blot it with a tissue.

00:07:30.050 --> 00:07:32.000
Once I'm happy with the shape of her lips,

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:33.720
I can move on to the cheeks.

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:36.123
I'm using a slightly
bigger paintbrush here.

00:07:38.380 --> 00:07:40.160
I always leave it slightly lighter

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:42.735
than I would like, because it dries dark.

00:07:46.430 --> 00:07:49.780
I'm using some white acrylic craft paint

00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:52.875
and very carefully filling in the teeth.

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:02.320
Now that her teeth are done,

00:08:02.320 --> 00:08:05.779
my last step is to fill in her eyebrows.

00:08:08.940 --> 00:08:10.950
Now that Felicity is finished,

00:08:10.950 --> 00:08:13.800
I've tied her hair into
her original hairstyle

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:16.200
with a little white ribbon in the back.

00:08:16.200 --> 00:08:18.220
I've put her in this purple dress.

00:08:18.220 --> 00:08:20.990
This is from a newer edition of Felicity.

00:08:20.990 --> 00:08:23.600
Now she is ready to go
on to her next owner

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:25.223
and be loved once again.

